# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD runs entrypoint.ps1, which starts sshd + WinRM, launches the
# vulnerable Jenkins 2.32.1 WAR as a DETACHED child java process, then execs an idle
# loop as PID 1. So:
#   * Jenkins is ALREADY serving on :8080 when the agent starts — verify.ps1's live
#     probes and 8080 regression have a running instance to hit, and the
#     "swapped the WAR on disk but never restarted" case stays detectable;
#   * PID 1 is the idle loop, so stopping/restarting java cannot kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must replace the WAR AND restart the running java
# process (not merely stage a new WAR on disk) — the vulnerable instance is already up.
